Issue: v8 strong mode in iojs 2.2.1 is not usable in a practical application

Problem:
if v8 strong mode is enabled by command line option --strong_mode and the app has "use strong", then the strong mode rules will not let the code use the 'arguments' pseudo-array. This is by design. It tells you 

SyntaxError: Please don't use 'arguments' in strong mode, use '...args' instead

However, currently the v8 version iojs uses does not yet support the ...args spread operator. if you use ...args you get an unexpected token error. 

```
// neither of these functions will compile in strong mode with iojs 2.2.1
"use strong";
function g() {
    let a = Array.prototype.slice.call(arguments);
    console.log(a.length);
}

function f(...args) {
  console.log(args.length);
}
```

