If present, the `error.cause` property is the underlying cause of the `Error`. It is used when catching an error and throwing a new one with a different
message or code in order to still have access to the original error. The `error.cause` property is typically set by calling
`new Error(message, { cause })`. It is not set by the constructor if the
`cause` option is not provided. This property allows errors to be chained. When serializing `Error` objects,
[`util.inspect()`][] recursively serializes `error.cause` if it is set. ```js
