* `statusCode` {number}
* `statusMessage` {string}
* `headers` {HTTP/2 Headers Object|HTTP/2 Raw Headers}
* Returns: {http2.Http2ServerResponse}
Sends a response header to the request. The status code is a 3-digit HTTP
status code, like `404`. The last argument, `headers`, are the response headers. Returns a reference to the `Http2ServerResponse`, so that calls can be chained. For compatibility with [HTTP/1][], a human-readable `statusMessage` may be
passed as the second argument. However, because the `statusMessage` has no
meaning within HTTP/2, the argument will have no effect and a process warning
will be emitted. ```js
