V8 only supports `Latin-1/ISO-8859-1` and `UTF16` as the underlying representation of a string. If the `content` uses `Latin-1/ISO-8859-1` as the underlying representation, this function will return true;
otherwise, it returns false. If this method returns false, that does not mean that the string contains some characters not in `Latin-1/ISO-8859-1`. Sometimes a `Latin-1` string may also be represented as `UTF16`.

```mjs
